{
  "name": "wall_crouch_peek",
  "note": "(anim-rework S5 keys, real-world standard, keyed by hand; never traced) Back to the wall, crouched peek at the edge ahead (the side-on posed frame, the wall on the LEFT; mirrored for the other side): the lean comes from the hips and the front (outside) knee: a split stance with the right foot forward (knee 106 deg over the toes) and the left knee low behind on the ball of its foot (104 deg), the pelvis 5 cm forward of the crouch and the trunk further over (pelvis 28, chest 48 deg), the head up and turned 12 deg toward the wall side to see round the edge; the right hand on the front knee for balance (palm down, wrist frame on every key), the left hand low by the shin. Held with two slow breaths and a small forward-back ease of 1.5 cm. Not mirrored. Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up). Pelvis offsets in cm from the standing rest. Arms: flex (+ forward, in the chest frame: the world angle is flex minus the chest pitch), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward; wrist (anim-rig, RIG.md) yaw / pitch / roll in the forearm frame, right hand as written, the left mirrored. Holstered arms; with a weapon drawn the arms stay procedural. Legs (the Blender preview and the track only: the game's feet come from the foot planner): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in toward the midline), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up).",
